<title>UK: UK drug shares hit record highs, ignore sterling.</title>
<headline>UK drug shares hit record highs, ignore sterling.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in leading UK pharmaceutical companies scored record highs on Friday, shrugging off this week's rally in sterling that undercut other industrial groups with large overseas earnings.</p>
<p>Analysts cited strength in their American Depository Receipts (ADRs) in New York overnight, healthy gains in the overall market, and recent positive research notes.</p>
</text>
